// Regression fixture for final-review Critical 1 (memory-audit-4e
// whole-branch review, probe P2): a runtime global-to-global text
// assignment. Originally (4e): `cl_free_globals` only ever covered a
// global's own INIT expression, never a later store in a handler/function
// body -- `p2G2 = p2G1` copies `p2G1`'s handle into `p2G2` (Ch3 reference
// semantics), then `cl_free_globals` froze both: SIGSEGV. The whole-program
// globals escape pre-pass (lower.cla's `lowRunGlobalsEscapePrepass`, Task
// 8's window-var trick reused for globals) fixed the crash by disqualifying
// both names from `cl_free_globals` (still true today -- that pass is
// Task 6's, untouched by ARC Task 4).
//
// ARC Task 4 (counted named-slot stores): `p2G2 = p2G1` is a NAMED-SLOT
// store (a global, same funnel as a local -- `lowCountedStore`) whose
// source is a bare identifier, non-birth -- retains `p2G1` FIRST, then
// releases `p2G2`'s OLD "two" handle. That release is real now (was, pre-
// Task-4, the permanent "orphan-on-overwrite" leak this comment used to
// describe as unfixable): `p2G2`'s original handle is properly freed the
// moment the store runs, confirmed against the emitted C (`rt_text_retain
// (cv_p2G1); rt_text_release(cv_p2G2); cv_p2G2 = cv_p2G1;`). Expected
// strict-mode leak count: 2 (see ../p2_global_assign.leaks, dropped from 4)
// -- `p2G1`'s shared "one" handle only (2 blocks): the store's own retain
// gave it rc==2, but `cl_free_globals` still never runs (both names stay
// disqualified there, Task 6's still-unmigrated slot class), so nothing
// ever decrements it back to zero. Not a bug -- a global's cleanup walk is
// explicitly out of this task's scope, staged for Task 6.

var p2G1: text = "one"
var p2G2: text = "two"

func runP2GlobalAssign() {
    p2G2 = p2G1
    alert("p2 done")
}
